                <pb facs="0213" n="105" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg105"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/8598: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacMurray</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-04-06T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1927—3
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received April 6—1:04
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>364. Yangtze Patrol commander telegraphed April 6 that Japanese plan to defend
                    their Concession at Hankow, and the present force there is two cruisers, four
                    destroyers and one gunboat.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
